# 2. LEARNING OBJECTIVES

This activity focuses on two important English language skills.

## A. READING

Students should be able to:

- Read a two-or-more-paragraph text about online safety.
- Identify important information.
- Identify who received a suspicious message.
- Identify who sent the message.
- Identify the prize mentioned.
- Identify the deadline.
- Identify personal information requested.
- Understand what the character did after receiving the message.

The original reading learning target must be preserved:

Students should correctly identify at least FOUR out of FIVE important details.

## B. WRITING

Students should be able to:

- Ask for simple advice.
- Give simple advice.
- Respond to simple advice.
- Use appropriate expressions such as:
  - What should I do?
  - Can you help me?
  - You should...
  - You shouldn't...
  - You could...
  - Thank you. I will...

The student must produce actual written responses.

Do not replace the writing activity with multiple-choice questions.

Maintain the original Year 5 English learning objectives, DSKP alignment and 60-minute lesson structure.

