## USE THIS EXACT READING PASSAGE

TITLE:

THE MYSTERY OF THE LUCKY MESSAGE

PARAGRAPH 1:

After school, Aina was using her phone to look for pictures for her school project. Suddenly, a notification appeared from a sender she did not recognise. The message displayed the name "Lucky Rewards" and said that Aina had won a free tablet. Aina was surprised because she had not entered any competition.

PARAGRAPH 2:

Under the message, there was a link. It told her to claim the prize before 6:00 p.m. that day. The page asked her to provide her full name, home address and phone number so the tablet could be delivered. Aina did not know who had sent the message, and the website address looked unfamiliar. She felt excited but also unsure about what to do.

PARAGRAPH 3:

Instead of clicking the link or replying, Aina stopped and showed the message to her mother. Her mother reminded her not to share personal information with unknown senders. She also advised Aina to ask a trusted adult whenever she received a suspicious message.

IMPORTANT:

Preserve this passage exactly.

Do not shorten it.

Do not replace it with a summary.

Do not remove paragraphs.

Use readable typography and appropriate line spacing.

The student must be able to refer to all three paragraphs throughout the comprehension activity.

